Kubeconfig for cluster test-clusters/data-cluster:

```yaml
apiVersion: v1
kind: Config
clusters:
- cluster:
    server: https://data-cluster-api.example.com:6443
  name: data-cluster
```

To use this kubeconfig:
1. Save the content between the ``` markers to a file (e.g., cluster-kubeconfig.yaml)
2. Use it with kubectl: kubectl --kubeconfig=cluster-kubeconfig.yaml get nodes
